{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1257267-solars-in-the-imperial-city","id":1257267,"title":"Solars in the Imperial City","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-25T15:11:17-07:00","id":1257267,"title":"Solars in the Imperial City","content":"I need some help preparing for my players exalted 3e session<br /> <br /> I have 5 solar PCs all of essence 2. They discovered that the Wyld Hunt was tracking them so they went to the library in Mahalanka and tricked Raksi into giving them access. They discovered the existence of the loom of fate and have decided to steal it. (They don't yet realize how big it is). At the end of last session they left lookshy with rented space on a fishing boat for the imperial city. <br /> <br /> What might happen to them when they get there? I guess my long term plan would be to have them find the inner sanctum and have to defeat the guardians at the gate to get into heaven where hijincks ensue before they discover the loom of fate itself. <br /> <br /> What trouble can I get them into on the way? Thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-25T15:59:54-07:00","id":1257270,"title":"","content":"Well, for trouble on the way, they're trying to sail across about 1300 miles of water on a fishing boat. That's basically like sailing from the west coast of Ireland all the way to the south tip of Greenland, or only about 25% shorter than the distance between Ireland and Newfoundland. So, it's a very long sea voyage, in a ship that I'd guess isn't very large - I would not generally assume that a &quot;fishing boat&quot; is very big. So the whole range of ocean encounters is available: great storms, sea monsters, pirates, and so on. <br /> <br /> Once they reach the Imperial City, things get even more interesting. Now, personally, I'm not an advocate of the idea that Sidereals can easily locate any given Exalt by using the Loom. At the very least, they have to know roughly who they're looking for, and actively do so - there's no &quot;Solar Alert&quot; setting that will warn them that random Solars are entering restricted territory. So, assuming they haven't already attracted hostile Sidereal attention, they should be able to at least enter the city without meeting immediate Exalted opposition.<br /> <br /> But that won't make it easy. First, there's going to be the regular challenges that anyone entering the Imperial City will face - they'll be expected to show some sort of permission to be there. If they're claiming to be foreigners, they'll probably be expected to state what their business is, and to have some amount of proof to back that up. And &quot;We're tourists&quot; will probably not fly for this - I doubt that the Realm in general, and the Imperial City in particular, accepts that as a valid reason for foreigners to visit, unless they're notably wealthy. And note that whatever story they spin will be examined more closely than usual, since they're coming from one of the Realm's traditional enemies, Lookshy.<br /> <br /> Once they get past the port authority, they have two major considerations: how to find the location of the Celestial Gate (and the sub-issue of how to <i>open</i> it), and how to live in the City while they're doing that. The second issue is probably more immediate - only Realm currency is likely to be accepted by most people in the Imperial City, so they'll have to convert any Threshold money they've got into that, if they're going to pay their way. That's probably expensive - I'd probably treat any such conversion as a purchase equal to the Resources level you want to have handy (barring some good negotiation with Bureaucracy), meaning that they'll probably have a bit less than their full Resources available, at least for the course of a story. Even once they get their money, they'll probably have to do some work to maintain their cover story - if they're merchants, they'll have to do some buying and selling, if they're religious pilgrims, they'll have to visit Immaculate shrines, and so on.<br /> <br /> The issue of finding the Celestial Gate can be complicated or simple, depending on how you want to play it. If someone has an appropriate Lore background, I'd allow a roll to declare a fact to place the location. If no one has the Lore background required, or you just want to draw this part out more, you could handle this as an extended roll, requiring rolls against Lore, Investigation, or Occult, probably with an interval of a day or so, until they hit whatever threshold you assign. Personally, I'd make the difficulty of the roll fairly high (4 or 5), but only require a fairly limited threshold (probably 5-10 successes). I think that makes the most sense - it takes someone with a lot of knowledge or ability to deduce to find a Gate in the first place, but if you <i>do</i> know the signs to look for, it actually doesn't take too long. <br /> <br /> No matter how they find the location, it will definitely be defended, even if that isn't super-obvious. Heaven doesn't want people just stumbling into it by accident. So I'd place it in a building where it doesn't look unusual for a bunch of guards to be wandering around, and one where spirits travelling in and out aren't completely implausible either. That suggests an Immaculate shrine to me, though other good candidates might be a location in the Imperial Bureaucracy, or possibly something maintained by one of the Great Houses.<br /> <br /> Of course, the party will have to do all of this while being very, <i>very</i> careful not to flare their animas. This is the heart of the Immaculate Philosophy - <i>everybody</i> is going to know the signs of Anathema. Just a caste mark should be enough to set off a countdown to a Wyld Hunt showing up, and not a long one, either. Basically, anyone who witnesses any level of anima is going to have to be infallibly dealt with if they don't want that.<br /> <br /> A question in general - do the players or the characters know that there's more than one Celestial Gate? Because there are, and probably virtually <i>all</i> of them are easier for a bunch of Solars to access than the one in the Imperial City. Are the characters going to this one because its the only one they know, but the players are aware, and just want to have the fun of infiltrating a heavily-defended enemy stronghold? If so, that's fine. But if the players don't realize there's other options, you might want to inform them <i>before</i> they get to the Imperial City, because they're likely to be resentful if they find out there were many easier options to get to Heaven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-25T16:35:43-07:00","id":1257276,"title":"","content":"You said the Wyld Hunt is already in pursuit, how known are they to it? Like does the Wyld Hunt just have the reports of 5 anathema in the area they were in, or has the circle been made?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-25T19:14:01-07:00","id":1257295,"title":"","content":"Wow so that sounds good. I'll have a sea monster attack to start. Then when they arrive they will have to find a celestial gate which will be challenging and somewhere super protected. The current wyld hunt doesn't know where they are. They are being formed and saw an animal flare from two of the exalted somehow tied to raksis thread in the loom. As far as the wyld hunt knows there are two anathema and they are on the periphery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T05:58:41-07:00","id":1257346,"title":"","content":"The loom isn't going to be easy to get to even if they're in yushan. I would read yushan or 1e sidereals to get a scope of how far a gate is from the loom as well as the kind of defenses and threats there are. Get to yu-shan is one thing compared to moving through it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T08:03:16-07:00","id":1257366,"title":"","content":"Step 1: Get to the Imperial City<br /> Step 2: Find a Celestial gate<br /> Step 3: Enter Heaven<br /> Step 4: Find the Loom<br /> Step 5: steal the Loom<br /> Step 6:....<br /> Step 7: Profit<br /> <br /> It's worth noting that this process goes from merely difficult to nigh-on impossible with steadily increasing likelihood of running afoul of the Wyld Hunt/the Bronze faction. You've got some pretty arrogant essence 2 Solars in your party... of wait, nm, that's pretty much every Solar PC ever. Carry on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T11:46:32-07:00","id":1257411,"title":"","content":"Well my players don't realize that the loom is in Yu Shan. They just determined that if the wyld hunt comes from the realm, the realm must have the loom. They also think the loom is hand sized and I'm not sure why. It should be quite a shock when they realize the loom is fifteen miles long and located In heaven.<br /> <br /> I think the difficulty for me as a first time exalted St is what actualy stands in their way? I imagine there will be realm guards. Maybe some heavenly guards on the gate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T12:20:39-07:00","id":1257415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1257267-solars-in-the-imperial-city?p=1257411#post1257411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well my players don't realize that the loom is in Yu Shan. They just determined that if the wyld hunt comes from the realm, the realm must have the loom. They also think the loom is hand sized and I'm not sure why. It should be quite a shock when they realize the loom is fifteen miles long and located In heaven.<br /> <br /> I think the difficulty for me as a first time exalted St is what actualy stands in their way? I imagine there will be realm guards. Maybe some heavenly guards on the gate.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are several celestial lions guarding the gate and if they try to force their way in it becomes an army. OOC i would probably disuade them or IC i would perhaps have them find a book on yu-shan that details these things to at least they won't try something akin to picking a fight with billions of gods and a bulk of the sidereals. The loom is the fundemental underpinning of creation. It's not something you can can casually steal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T12:23:38-07:00","id":1257416,"title":"","content":"If they know about the Loom, do they know about the Maidens?<br /> <br /> *whistles* If you want a comprehensive list....<br /> <br /> 1: The Imperial City is full to the brim with Dragon Blooded. It's the heart of the Realm, and therefor the point most of their elders congregate. So all the Great Houses have forces nearby, most major buildings have dedicated security forces, and the Imperial Force: the Realm policing unit charged with arresting Dragon Blooded is nearby. There are hundreds of powerful Dragonblooded nearby should the PCs start drawing attention to themselves, Plus since it's known for politicking, everyone in authority is likely going to be suspicious.<br /> <br /> Now, branching path. Do they work out that it's in Heaven, or does that pass them by?<br /> 2a, The most likely spot for them to investigate is the Scarlet Empress' palace, and the attached Imperial Manse. This is guarded by the Legion of Silence: a group of sorcerously created supersoldiers, and the defenses within the manse proper are all first age stuff. It's literally the most epic dungeon in Creation: even for Solars, the traps within will be difficult. After all, Solars built them. Powerful autometa, tricky puzzle locks and sorcery designed to get them out of there... nothing's off the table<br /> <br /> This... kinda ends here. Unless your Solars are willing to take on the most powerful Dragon Blooded in the Dynasty/the toughest dungeon of them all, this will likely prove a dead end. <br /> <br /> <br /> 2b: Assuming they work out they need to get to heaven, they need to find a Yu Shan gate. The gods know about them, so they'll need to find a god and talk it into giving them directions to the nearest one. Could be easy could be hard depending on your circle's composition<br /> <br /> 3: Upon finding a gate, you go through the creation side and there's a passageway leading to a second gate that opens onto Heaven. This second gate is guarded by Celestial Lions who'll ask the PCs what buisness they have in Yu Shan<br /> <br /> 4: Getting to Yu Shan, the PCs will have to find a way to reach the Locus of Heavenly Design. Keep in mind Yu Shan is massive: it's the size of the Blessed Isle. Gods mostly use the canal system to get around.<br /> <br /> 5: Once they reach the Locus.... well, no one really planned on anyone trying to steal the whole loom. There'll be some more Celestial Lions around, but so long as no one does anything malicious, they'll probably get in fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T12:31:11-07:00","id":1257417,"title":"","content":"... I am massively interested in learning how this campaign goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T12:39:14-07:00","id":1257418,"title":"","content":"Isn't there also a trick about opening the gates? I know spirits are supposed to be able to get in easily enough, but I think ,at least in 2E, you needed sorcerery to get the gate open on the Creation side. So depending on how difficult it is to get the gate open without the help of a spirit that might also influence the security. Afterall if it requires a sorcerous ritual taking an hour to open the door without a god then it can probably just be folded into normal patrol routines and whatever security the area would necessitate as it would be unlikely for someone to open the door quickly without it moving into DB territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T13:45:25-07:00","id":1257435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1257267-solars-in-the-imperial-city?p=1257418#post1257418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't there also a trick about opening the gates? I know spirits are supposed to be able to get in easily enough, but I think ,at least in 2E, you needed sorcerery to get the gate open on the Creation side. So depending on how difficult it is to get the gate open without the help of a spirit that might also influence the security. Afterall if it requires a sorcerous ritual taking an hour to open the door without a god then it can probably just be folded into normal patrol routines and whatever security the area would necessitate as it would be unlikely for someone to open the door quickly without it moving into DB territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... Interesting note. You're quite right: canonically, you need a spell that could allow you to enter a spirit's sanctum, or an equivelent artifact/charm. I don't believe those exist in Ex3 yet, but assuming mortals pass back and forth, finding an artifact is plausible. Failing that, it looks like you could have a friendly god/elemental open the door for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T13:52:49-07:00","id":1257438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1257267-solars-in-the-imperial-city?p=1257411#post1257411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well my players don't realize that the loom is in Yu Shan. </div> </div> </div> </div>A question - are your players all completely new to Exalted? I don't think all players should be, like, immersed in 100% of the lore, but this sounds to me like stuff that even people who are vaguely familiar with the setting might be aware of.<br /> <br /> Again, I'd <i>strongly</i> suggest chatting with your players <i>before</i> they get to the Imperial City, and make sure they're all on the same page here. It's fine if the players are aware this is likely to be much harder than the characters expect, and think that's part of the fun. But if it's the players who don't realize this, and are surprised when it's harder, you will probably get some pushback. Especially if any of the characters have abilities like Lore that they could roll to know about stuff like this - that's likely to provoke complaints of &quot;my character should have known that this was a dumb idea. Now <i>I</i> feel dumb.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the difficulty for me as a first time exalted St is what actualy stands in their way? I imagine there will be realm guards. Maybe some heavenly guards on the gate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both of those, for sure. Like I said, the Gate's likely to be in a place that's already heavily guarded for non-Heavenly reasons, so there should be mortal guards stationed there, with very high stats. Personally, for those, I'd start with the &quot;Elite Troops&quot; Quick Character stats (Exalted Core, p. 497), bump up all their die pools by 1, and further increase their Read Intentions and Senses pools by <i>another</i> 1, since they'd be trained particularly to read people and observe them. Besides those, there would also be at least a couple, if not more, Dragonblooded commanders. I'd suggest using the Experienced Dragon-blood QC (Ex3 Core, p. 544) as the commander of the guard, and the Young Dynast QC (p. 541) for the rest. Or, if the gate is in an Immaculate Philosophy building, use various Immaculate QCs (pp. 541-544). In that case, in fact, you could easily justify a whole Hearth of Immaculates as the leaders of the guard, with additional Dragon-bloods to boot, plus mortal monks, of course.<br /> <br /> In addition to the mortals and Dragon-Blooded defenders, there could possibly be some spirit defenders on the Realm side of the Gate as well. They'd have to be spirits who were able to reliably disguise themselves as humans, but that's not too difficult to find. Any given &quot;mortal&quot; could actually have much more impressive stats, and suddenly start breaking out some impressive magic when the Solars reveal themselves. For that, I'd use stats similar to the Storm Mother QC (Exalted Core pp. 513-514, though I'd suggest changing the merits and charms around). <br /> <br /> Once they're through the Gate, the spiritual opposition will ramp <i>right</i> up. As mentioned above, those will start with a few Celestial Lions, and get worse from there, as reinforcements arrive. The <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/897582-qc-the-codex\">first post of this thread</a> has some decent stats for Celestial Lions. Other spirits you'll have to make up, but the Gates are a big deal - a serious fight could probably draw out someone as potent as a Lesser Elemental Dragon, if it went on long enough.<br /> <br /> Of course, once they're through the Gate, things will only get tougher - the Loom is not immediately accessible from any of the Gates, so the party will have to cross Yu-Shan (which is as big as the entire Blessed Isle, remember!) to get to one of the Maiden's Houses, which each contain portals to the Loom's sub-dimension. There, they'll have to deal with <i>more</i> defenders, which should certainly include high-Essence Sidereals, in addition to all the other spirits.<br /> <br /> Frankly, fighting all of Heaven sounds like a losing proposition to me, even for Solars. They'd be better off if, when they enter the Gate, they can convince the Lions there that they have legitimate business in Heaven. That generally requires being invited by a god, a high-ranked elemental, or a high-ranked Sidereal, so they'd better be able to get that, or be <i>very</i> good at lying (and remember that the Celestial Lions have some good lie-detection abilities too). Getting that permission will allow them into Heaven and probably let them move about reasonably easily, but getting into one of the Maidens' Houses to access the Loom is another matter. Also remember that many spirits will have the inherent ability to gauge what sort of beings they are (various versions of Measure the Wind), and will be curious and/or hostile to humans walking about, so it will be very hard to go unnoticed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T14:54:36-07:00","id":1257445,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering if any of them actually know what a loom is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T18:51:04-07:00","id":1257483,"title":"","content":"I don't think the current plan from the players is to fight their way there. They realize the realm is bad news. Their plan is to sneak in steal the loom and run before the realm realizes they took it. Of course this plan won't survive impact with reality.<br /> <br /> I imagine they will find the offices where the wyld hunt info is coming from assume the loom is there. Sneak or fight their way inside and realize it's actually a path to another realm. Either retreat and research a way to open the gate or convince a god to let them in. Once they arrive and see that they can't just steal a massive building? Well that will be a real interesting moment.<br /> <br /> Quite frankly I don't know ow why they think a loom that has strands for all mortals in creation would be hand sized... But you know. I think it will be a great moment in campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T07:45:34-07:00","id":1257568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1257267-solars-in-the-imperial-city?p=1257483#post1257483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quite frankly I don't know ow why they think a loom that has strands for all mortals in creation would be hand sized...</div> </div> </div> </div>See, when you say this, it's a warning sign to me. I think that an important skill, when you're running a game, is, when your players are doing something you think is obviously stupid, to stop and ask yourself &quot;<i>why</i> are they doing something stupid, and is it because I haven't given them enough information?&quot;. It's important to remember that the Storyteller will pretty much always have more information than the players do - even if they've read all the setting material extensively, your version of the setting may well be different. Furthermore, you're the channel that all in-character knowledge flows through. You get to decide what their characters would know. So, you should know why the characters think the Loom could possibly be that small - is it because they're all ignorant peasants or just completely uneducated in the larger world of Creation? Or have you not given out information that they should logically have? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you know. I think it will be a great moment in campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's possible, but it's also possible it won't, and will, in fact, be a major source of irritation and aggravation to your players. As a player, one of the things I find <i>most</i> irritating is when I make decisions that turn out to be based on wrong information when my character would have logically have known the right information, or even had a chance to work it out that I never got. It creates the feeling that my character is just an idiot, which isn't very fun. This is only reinforced if the GM then goes on to say how ridiculous they found my actions, because <i>they</i> were the one who withheld information from me. We find anecdotes like the <a href=\"https://www.netfunny.com/rhf/jokes/98/Jul/gazebo.html\" target=\"_blank\">Gazebo Story</a> amusing, but bear in mind they probably weren't that funny to the player they happened to. <br /> <br /> Remember, if any of the PCs have any dots in relevant Abilities, like Lore (to know general history and the nature of things), Craft (to know how artifacts generally work), or Occult (general practical magical knowledge), it's okay to feed the players a hint or two - you can call for a (Wits + Lore) roll and, if it gets any successes, say &quot;You know, thinking about this, something that dictates the fate of a whole world might not be that small. Maybe you should do a bit of research before we get there.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T08:00:24-07:00","id":1257571,"title":"","content":"See, now I'm imagining that they find a Getimian and realize that he's got a miniature loom inside his ribcage and attempt to kidnap him on the assumption that <i>he </i>is the Loom of Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T20:16:57-07:00","id":1257708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1257267-solars-in-the-imperial-city?p=1257571#post1257571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, now I'm imagining that they find a Getimian and realize that he's got a miniature loom inside his ribcage and attempt to kidnap him on the assumption that <i>he </i>is the Loom of Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the horrified looks if they think the Immaculates put it there, &quot;Oh my god they're shoving spider robots in people to manipulate destiny!&quot;<br /> <br /> As far as it goes, it wouldn't be too bad an idea to workshop with the group just to make sure you're all on the same page and that maybe check what they know. I mean for all we know they're figuring the loom is massive, but that its stored inside an extradimensional space that they can steal easily. Plus you can get some extra ideas based on what the players are figuring, like if they're thinking the loom is like a central hub through which information is disseminated and compiled for the Wyld Hunt then they're going to be expecting very different thing than if they think the Loom is some sort of oracular scrying pool capable of fortelling the future and that the Immaculates can sometimes use it well enough to get a read on Anathema they'll want to hunt. <br /> <br /> Hell an important point do they think its actually a loom like in Wanted? See I'm not gonna say the PCs should know that the Loom is probably huge because they're from Creation because I honestly don't believe the literal workings of Fate are known enough that most people would know that the Loom isn't some metaphor or that it isn't the freaking stars since those can be used to tell the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-28T09:13:35-07:00","id":1257785,"title":"","content":"Well session is tonight! I will let you all know how it goes. I will start with a sea monster sent by raksi to retrieve them. Then have them run into an old friend in the imperial city who belongs to house tepet. Follow that up with finding the building they need and do an infiltration of some sort. Somehow get past the golden lions into Yu Shan. I doubt we will get through all that tonight so I might have a few more weeks to figure it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-28T10:29:20-07:00","id":1257795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1257267-solars-in-the-imperial-city?p=1257416#post1257416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they know about the Loom, do they know about the Maidens?<br /> <br /> *whistles* If you want a comprehensive list....<br /> <br /> 1: The Imperial City is full to the brim with Dragon Blooded. It's the heart of the Realm, and therefor the point most of their elders congregate. So all the Great Houses have forces nearby, most major buildings have dedicated security forces, and the Imperial Force: the Realm policing unit charged with arresting Dragon Blooded is nearby. There are hundreds of powerful Dragonblooded nearby should the PCs start drawing attention to themselves, Plus since it's known for politicking, everyone in authority is likely going to be suspicious.<br /> <br /> Now, branching path. Do they work out that it's in Heaven, or does that pass them by?<br /> 2a, The most likely spot for them to investigate is the Scarlet Empress' palace, and the attached Imperial Manse. This is guarded by the Legion of Silence: a group of sorcerously created supersoldiers, and the defenses within the manse proper are all first age stuff. It's literally the most epic dungeon in Creation: even for Solars, the traps within will be difficult. After all, Solars built them. Powerful autometa, tricky puzzle locks and sorcery designed to get them out of there... nothing's off the table<br /> <br /> This... kinda ends here. Unless your Solars are willing to take on the most powerful Dragon Blooded in the Dynasty/the toughest dungeon of them all, this will likely prove a dead end.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2b: Assuming they work out they need to get to heaven, they need to find a Yu Shan gate. The gods know about them, so they'll need to find a god and talk it into giving them directions to the nearest one. Could be easy could be hard depending on your circle's composition</div> </div> </div> </div>2c the effectively conquered the realm by accidently taking over the Imperial Mance and the Sword of Creation!! if the take the path of it must be the imperial mance this is a very real sidetrack that might happen just because of the escalating defences they might think that it does actually contain the Loom<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11701-fiikragg","name":"Fiikragg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11701_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-29T00:14:29-07:00","id":1257924,"title":"","content":"Wait why is a fishing boat going from one end of the Inland Sea to the other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-30T01:35:39-07:00","id":1258146,"title":"","content":"Bit late to this party, but...<br /> <br /> If the Wyld Hunt is *already* tracking the Circle, then this is a <b>horrible</b> idea for them to try to pull off. Sneaking into the heart of Dragon-Blooded/Bronze Faction territory would be hard enough if they weren't actively looking for you, but if the Sidereals in the WH already <i>have</i> a lock on you...<br /> <br /> You probably could have headed this off by just having the Library accurately describe the Loom for them, or at least mention that there are dozens of Heavenly Gates, far less guarded that they are passing up in order to go to the most dangerous one. Should they somehow survive all this, actually getting into and around Heaven isn't that hard so long as they have an Eclipse with them, but if not...<br /> <br /> See, this is the sort of thing that <i>seems</i> downright suicidal, but these <i>are</i> Solars, so part of me is strongly expecting you to come by tomorrow and tell us, &quot;Well, they pulled it off...&quot;!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-30T01:41:06-07:00","id":1258148,"title":"","content":"Meh, just sneak into the Imperial City via the Underworld. That's what my PCs did. They went through the Labyrinth to Stygia, then broke through into Creation, hid in a park, scoped out the Imperial palace for a day, then broke in. Sidereals can't track you through the Underworld.<br /> <br /> RadioFreeDeath, your PCs are Essence 5 right? Go for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-30T01:52:10-07:00","id":1258151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1257267-solars-in-the-imperial-city?p=1258148#post1258148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh, just sneak into the Imperial City via the Underworld. That's what my PCs did. They went through the Labyrinth to Stygia, then broke through into Creation, hid in a park, scoped out the Imperial palace for a day, then broke in. Sidereals can't track you through the Underworld.<br /> <br /> RadioFreeDeath, your PCs are Essence 5 right? Go for it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 5 PCs, at Essence *2*. Yeah, if they were all at 5, then just go nuts!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Not sure how it works in 3E, what with the Shroud...In previous editions, you pretty much couldn't do that as there are no Shadowlands on the Blessed Isle. Well, there's probably some Necromancy spell or other that can do it, maybe. Wonder when we'll get solid info on the Shroud and how it works?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-30T02:08:31-07:00","id":1258156,"title":"","content":"This was 2nd ed. They hired a necromancer in Stygia.<br /> <br /> Possibly this is a bit late for these PCs, who are already on the Fishing Boat.<br /> <br /> So, RadioFreeDeath, how'd it go?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-05T13:45:12-07:00","id":1259120,"title":"","content":"Sorry! Its been a week. I need to catch everyone up on where we are at. <br /> <br /> <br /> So my PCs were attacked by a sea witch as they crossed the sea. The sea Witch had been dispatched by Raksi to bring them back as she was unhappy that they had fled Mahalanka after getting into the library sessions ago. They convinced the sea witch to remove the curse from them and let them go.<br /> <br /> Upon arrival in the Imperial City, one of the players ran into Tepet Ajava (A 4 point ally) a dragon blooded they had known from their time in Llinowan at the very beginning of the campaign. He was unaware that the PCs were exalted and he was in town in an attempt to convince the realm to help the Llinowan against the Bull of the North who was massing forces in Halta to invade Llinowan. He invited them to stay with him in the Tepet wing of the Palace. He is not having much luck as parties jockey for power. They learned about the imperial palace and the disappearance of the empress a few years before. <br /> <br /> The Night Caste also received attention from the all seeing eye but showed the letter he recieved from them to the Zenith Caste so both are now marked for death. <br /> <br /> The players did some research and determined that they believed the loom to be located in a temple. <br /> <br /> Now I have to take a quick break to explain about a legendary artifact the PCs have. Its one main doorknob and 5 secondary doorknobs. Each of the secondary doorknobs can be placed somewhere in creation on a door and after attuning for one day that door now opens to the main doorknob wherever it is anywhere in creation. The players have one doorknob in Chanta. So they devised a plan. The eclipse caste crossed to Chanta and visited the Bull of the North. He convinced him that he had found a cave that would give a small number of soldiers access directly to the heart of the realm. The bull decided to use the &quot;cave&quot; (really just the artifact created door to the imperial city) to send across spies and saboteurs into the imperial city. However, one of the other members of the Bull's circle began to figure out that the &quot;cave&quot; was really something else and that the eclipse was playing them. The PCs panicked and the Night cast snuck in and stole the doorknob keeping the cave open after a small group of the Bull's soldiers and made it through and shut the gate down. However the eclipse caste was trapped on the Bull's side. The bull angry at the double cross sent soldiers to capture the eclipse who at the beginning of this session is about to fight his way out of the Bull's ambush.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile The other 4 PCs waited until the Bull's soldiers in the imperial city had started a fire in the outer slums. As the monks rushed towards the slum to help with the spreading conflagaration they PCs snuck by the few remaining guards into the temple. The Dawn caste was spotted but quickly and quietly defeated the guards before they could raise the alarm. The PCs made their way to a room at the center of the temple where they discovered a portal to Yu- Shan. ( I handwaved opening the portal for narrative purposes) Two Golden Lions stepped through the gate and informed the PCs that they would not be allowed entry. <br /> <br /> Thats where we ended the session. So one PC is trapped halfway across creation at the mercy of the Bull. The other PCs are deciding if they can convince the Lions to let them pass or whether they will try to storm the gate.<br /> <br /> So for tonights session:<br /> <br /> I'll start with the Bull of the North and the Eclipse. The eclipse will either escape and be pursued or will be captured and have to find a way to escape or convince the bull not to kill him. He knows that if he can get to Chanta he can get back to the rest of the circle. And the circle will quickly learn what trouble he is in.<br /> <br /> The other PCs will have to find a way into heaven where they will have to find a way to find the loom. Upon realizing how big the loom is, things will get creative. If they get too stuck I like the idea of a gentimian who can fit the entire loom inside itself. I may create an opening there. I need to remember to allow the players to realize the destroying or damaging the loom would be a really bad idea. <br /> <br /> I also ended up with a split group which will be a serious problem. I didn't expect them to panic and create the massive division. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile I think realm agents will quickly capture or kill most of the Bull's agents. Once they realize what the Bull did I imagine the hammer will come down quickly on the PCs if they stick around. <br /> <br /> It might also be a good session to introduce the players to the existence of the sidereals and their factional disputes. <br /> <br /> Anyways in 5 hours session starts!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-05T21:38:59-07:00","id":1259181,"title":"","content":"Looking forward to hearing more!<br /> <br /> On a more general note, what are some ways Solars might get tumbled deep in Imperial territory? Unless they're actively using Essence/Charms, Solars are basically just normal mortals. Their chances of evading capture or even notice are pretty good, esp with Stealth and/or Socialize Charms. There are powers that detect even subtle charm use, but (at least in prior editions) the DB version of that only works by touch, so unless they happen to be using it when they just happen to bump into a Solar...The Sidereal version lets them literally *hear* Essence in use, but the odds of running into a Sid are really low (hopefully, they're not using their &quot;odds raising&quot; Excellency to look for you!). So, if you were getting antsy that your PCs are taking it for granted that they are TOO safe in Scarlet Town, how might you shake them up a bit?<br /> <br /> BTW, do powers that detect Charms/Essence use work on Permanent Charms, like Ox Body Tech? I wouldn't think so, but I could be wrong...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-06T01:06:54-07:00","id":1259202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1257267-solars-in-the-imperial-city?p=1259181#post1259181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless they're actively using Essence/Charms, Solars are basically just normal mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might take another look at Measure the Wind, there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-06T02:51:28-07:00","id":1259212,"title":"","content":"That's about the only thing that would work though, so unless the dragonbloods have gods or bound demons scanning for anathema you're good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 10-06-2018, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-06T03:26:03-07:00","id":1259214,"title":"","content":"I think the issue is that Solars can just walk around like regular mortals, doing regular stuff, and it's pretty undetectable... but they don't. They cause problems, kill people, lead uprisings, get into fights with the guard, glow all over the place and give themselves away.<br /> <br /> A Solar circle could infiltrate the Imperial City by just becoming regular merchants, merchanting in on a regular ship, selling some stuff, etc. But once they start causing trouble, as they inevitably will, that's when all those Dragonblood investigators start tracking them down.<br /> <br /> I have never seen a PC circle with the self-discipline to pose as mortals effectively for a long time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-06T03:41:10-07:00","id":1259215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1257267-solars-in-the-imperial-city?p=1259212#post1259212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That'a about the only thing that would work though, so unless the dragonbloods have gods or bound demons scanning for anathema you're good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Less that DBs &quot;have gods\u2026 scanning for Anathema,&quot; more that a person who looks or acts funny might draw the attention of an immaterial spirit, especially if their actions falls under his purview. The Immaculate Order's presence on the Isle is strong enough for even a god to pay lip service to it, especially if they might give him a festival day this year if he helps them catch some Anathema.<br /> <br /> I particularly would keep an eye out for PCs committing any murders; Bloody Hands are so much fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-06-2018, 08:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T10:27:30-07:00","id":1259617,"title":"","content":"Alright so last session my players worked it out. They sent just the eclipse into Yu Shan while the rest of the PCs bunkered down in House Tepet. <br /> <br /> The PC in the north called on his warstrider to break through the barbarians sent to stop him from the Bull of the North and fled into Llinowan where he met with Queen Arkasi and agreed to help defend Llinowan against Halta and the Bull.<br /> <br /> The Eclipse PC found the loom and realized it was unstealable. He did spy on some sidereals and discovered the existence of the bronze faction before escaping yu shan.<br /> <br /> The other PCs worked with house Tepet to try and get another expedition to go North and Stop the Bull in Llinowan.<br /> <br /> No one got murdered and no one flared anima so they stayed mostly under the radar.<br /> <br /> I have three weeks until next session and it will be after six months of downtime. The players have regrouped in Llinowan and are preparing to face off against the Bull of the North as he faces llinowan. Meanwhile House Tepet has persuaded houes Peleps to send a legion with their legion in a last ditch effort to stop the Bull after the Bull did so much damage to the Imperial City slums. However A wyld Hunt has been put together to find the PCs and the sidereals believe they are in the north, so a wyld hunt has attached itself to the expedition to the north.<br /> <br /> My plans for next session will probably be a big battle with the bull. The Realm forces will arrive sometime during the battle which might even the odds. However the players will find themselves the target of a wyld hunt from those who are ostenibly their allies. <br /> <br /> Right now I am doing tallies of the forces for each army. I need to stat up the Bull's circle for 3e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}